From 55cf5c70e9cdf6843f27bf5d0fcb998c9e18ea90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kirn Gill II <segin2005@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 00:22:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 30/98] contrib/glib1: port GLib 1.2.10 (GTK+ 1.2 base library)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Source-only patch-series port.  fetch.sh downloads + SHA-verifies the
GNOME tarball, borrows the substrate-patched config.sub/config.guess
from the binutils port, and applies the series; build.sh cross-configures
(autoconf 2.13, so cross run-tests are preseeded via env glib_cv_*/ac_cv_*)
and stages shared + static into dist-glib1, with glib-config for the
gtk1 port to consume.

Patches:
- 0001-configure-cross: make the "ANSI library prototypes" and "POLL*
  sysdef" run-probes cross-safe (substrate <sys/poll.h> matches glib's
  defaults).
- 0002-glib-h-modern-gcc: G_GNUC_PRETTY_FUNCTION must be a string literal
  for the g_warning("..." ...) concat (gcc16 won't concat
  __PRETTY_FUNCTION__); drop the obsolete __asm__ __const__ qualifier
  from the i386 byteswap macros.
- 0003-ltconfig-substrate-shared: canonicalize host_os=substrate to
  linux-gnu in the 2001-era ltconfig so it reuses the full linux ELF
  shared-library profile (version_type=linux, soname, library_names)
  instead of falling through to static-only — same effect modern
  libtool already has for substrate.

build.sh post-patches each .so's OSABI byte to ELFOSABI_SUBSTRATE (0x40),
as the X stack ports do.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
